            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Christopher Sides",
                        "email": "christopher.sides@hpe.com",
                        "username": "csides-hpe"
                    },
                    "message": "I decided to split out the (admittedly simple) support for tachless fans into a separate PR @ 83209: fan path disambiguation+ | https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/dbus-sensors/+/83209\n\nin hopes it'll be easier to get reviewers to review stuff if I can truthfully advertise on discord as \"there's no functional changes happening in this code, it could all be classified as logical tidying up\" :)\n\nThis PR now *only* includes the functional change needed for tachless fan support."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/fan/FanMain.cpp",
                    "line": 230,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ChauLy-Vietnam",
                        "email": "chaul@amperecomputing.com",
                        "username": "chaul-ampere"
                    },
                    "message": "pwmPath?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/fan/FanMain.cpp",
                    "line": 239,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Christopher Sides",
                        "email": "christopher.sides@hpe.com",
                        "username": "csides-hpe"
                    },
                    "message": "If the output path fanN_input exists, then it's a standard fan, so return the fanN_input path.\n\nIF the file doesn't exist, it's a tachless fan, and TachSensor can be passed the 'pwmN' path to be used as a kind of 'virtual tachSensor' by phosphor-pid-control.\n\nNo other logical changes required for basic tachless fan support."
                }
